00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:09,750
A funny movie about getting serious.

2
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:13,500
Crossing Delancey is a comedy, romance film directed by Joan Micklin Silver.

3
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:17,250
Thirty-something Isabelle spends her time going from her tiny, solitary West
Side apartment to that of her grandmother on the Lower East Side.

4
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:21,000
While her grandmother plots to find her a romantic match, Isabelle is courted by a married, worldly
author, Anton, yet can't seem to shake the down-to-earth appeal of Sam, a pickle vendor.

5
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:24,750
Isabelle Grossman, played by Amy Irving.

6
00:36:22,500 --> 00:36:28,500
Sam Posner, played by Peter Riegert.

7
00:42:26,250 --> 00:42:32,250
Bubbie Kantor, played by Reizl Bozyk.

8
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Anton Maes, played by Jeroen Krabbé.

9
00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:39,750
Hannah Mandelbaum, played by Sylvia Miles.

10
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
Lionel, played by George Martin.

11
01:06:41,250 --> 01:06:47,250
Crossing Delancey is a 1988 American romantic comedy film adapted by  Susan Sandler
from her play of the same name, and directed by Joan Micklin Silver.

12
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
It stars Amy Irving and Peter Riegert.

13
01:18:48,750 --> 01:18:54,750
The film also features performances from Reizl Bozyk, David
Hyde-Pierce, Sylvia Miles and Rosemary Harris.

14
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
Amy Irving was nominated for a Golden Globe for the film, for Best
Actress in a Motion Picture - Comedy or Musical.

15
01:30:56,250 --> 01:31:02,250
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
